{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Gerrit change 1430 pushed — and the APPLY is NOT done\n\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1430 — `9baf: wire SNS actions on two mute alarms`.\n\n**What is in the change (4 files):**\n- `monitoring_s4b.tf` — `voter_errors` gains `alarm_actions` + `ok_actions` -> `aws_sns_topic.alerts.arn`.\n- `monitoring_s5.tf` — `replication_errors`, the sibling, gains the same. Scope expansion is\n  deliberate and was folded into this ticket's description BEFORE the plan-review attestation was\n  earned, so the reviewer certified the two-alarm scope.\n- `monitoring_1fa8.tf` — the 'UNLIKE S4b it WIRES SNS' comment corrected; it had documented the\n  convention from the single instance that violated it.\n- `tests/unit/test_alarm_actions_terraform.py` — NEW guard, 5 tests.\n\n**Guard behaviour:** parses every `aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm` block under `infra/terraform/`\n(masking comments, strings and heredocs so a brace or a prose mention cannot fool it) and fails on\nany block without `alarm_actions`; a second test does the same for `ok_actions`. An alarm that must\nstay silent needs `# rebar:allow-actionless-alarm: <reason>` in its block — silence never passes.\n\n**The anti-vacuity assertion caught a real bug in its first minute.** The initial parser matched the\nresource header against the masked text, where quoted strings are blanked — so it found ZERO blocks.\n`test_every_alarm_declares_alarm_actions` PASSED VACUOUSLY while the `>= 13` assertion failed loudly\nand exposed it. Recorded because it is direct evidence for the 34c2 / 8a5e / 1909 pattern: without\nthe count assertion this guard would have shipped green and worthless.\n\n**Verification:** RED first, naming exactly `monitoring_s4b.tf:voter_errors` and\n`monitoring_s5.tf:replication_errors`; GREEN after. Mutation A: re-deleting s4b's `alarm_actions`\nreturns it to RED. Mutation B: pointing the parser at an empty dir fails the anti-vacuity assertion\ninstead of passing. `terraform fmt -check` clean; `terraform validate` -> Success (so\n`aws_sns_topic.alerts.arn` genuinely resolves in both files). `make lint` + `make typecheck` pass.\n\n**Parity sweep:** no CloudWatch alarm is created anywhere outside `infra/terraform/` — no\n`put-metric-alarm` in any script, and `infra/terraform-github` has none. HCL is the only channel,\nso the guard covers the entire surface.\n\n## OPEN RESIDUAL — the alarms STILL notify nobody\n\nRead-only `describe-alarms` at this moment still returns 0 actions for BOTH\n`rebar-gerrit-voter-errors` and `rebar-gerrit-replication-errors` (the other 11 rebar-* alarms each\nhave 1). **Merging change 1430 will not change that.** Per [rebar:1c39-96d4-8f9e-4d38] the Terraform\ndrift check does not gate a Gerrit change, so this lands and reads as done while production is\nunchanged.\n\nI am NOT running the apply: it mutates shared AWS infrastructure and this ticket records apply as\noperator-run. (For accuracy: AWS credentials ARE present in this environment — account 896586841071,\nuser joe_frontier — so the blocker is authorisation and scope, not missing credentials.)\n\n**Therefore this ticket stays OPEN.** Two of its acceptance criteria are unmet and cannot be met by\nmerging HCL:\n- [ ] the change is APPLIED and live `describe-alarms` shows non-empty `AlarmActions`/`OKActions`;\n- [ ] one FORCED notification observed end-to-end (`set-alarm-state ALARM` -> subscriber received it).\n\nOperator steps to finish it:\n    terraform -chdir=infra/terraform apply     # expect exactly 2 alarms changed, no other diff\n    aws cloudwatch describe-alarms --alarm-names rebar-gerrit-voter-errors rebar-gerrit-replication-errors\n    aws cloudwatch set-alarm-state --alarm-name rebar-gerrit-voter-errors --state-value ALARM --state-reason 9baf-delivery-proof\n    # confirm the email actually ARRIVED, then let it return to OK\n\nDo not close this ticket on the merge alone."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785920753075648001,"uuid":"ececea6a-82b8-47b8-b7dc-e2f02a3f3d89"}